---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Testimonials preview | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Three double-border testimonial card designs."
>
  <style>
    .preview-head {
      padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-5);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-head h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    }
    .preview-panel {
      padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-panel .panel-label {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }
    .preview-panel h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }

    /* Shared card shell: double border like .rate-card / .contact-card */
    .tcard {
      position: relative;
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper);
      padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    }
    .tcard::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 3px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .tcard .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    }
    .tcard .a {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* Photo / logo placeholder */
    .ph {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      background: rgba(169, 203, 208, 0.35);
      color: var(--muted);
      border: 1px dashed var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    /* ---- New A: double-border grid, photo on top ---- */
    .ta-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .ta-grid .tcard {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-4);
    }
    .ta-grid .ph {
      width: 56px;
      height: 56px;
      border-radius: 50%;
    }

    /* ---- New B: double-border grid, logo top-right ---- */
    .tb-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tb-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
      min-height: 220px;
    }
    .tb-top {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }
    .tb-top .ph-logo {
      width: 72px;
      height: 32px;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .tb-quote {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    }
    .tb-quote .q {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    /* ---- New C: double-border, stacked photo left ---- */
    .tc-stack {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tc-card .tcard-inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      align-items: center;
    }
    .tc-card .ph {
      width: 80px;
      height: 80px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .tc-card .q {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .tc-card .tcard-inner {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head preview-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Testimonials · iteration 2</p>
      <h1>Double-border cards, three layouts.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Same double border as the rates and contact form. A photo placeholder
        appears in each. Deprecated the earlier three.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>

  <!-- New A -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option A photo top grid">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">A · Grid, photo on top</p>
      <div class="ta-grid">
        <div class="tcard">
          <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Photo</span>
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard">
          <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Photo</span>
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard">
          <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Photo</span>
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- New B -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option B logo top-right grid">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">B · Grid, logo top-right</p>
      <div class="tb-grid">
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <div>
            <div class="tb-top">
              <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
              <span class="ph ph-logo" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tb-quote">
              <p class="q">
                Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
                decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make
                it, then she stays until it lands.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <div>
            <div class="tb-top">
              <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
              <span class="ph ph-logo" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tb-quote">
              <p class="q">
                She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the
                room hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that
                had never questioned the plan started asking which one thing
                mattered most.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <div>
            <div class="tb-top">
              <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
              <span class="ph ph-logo" aria-hidden="true">Logo</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tb-quote">
              <p class="q">
                The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to
                shipped code in the same week. She brought our AI story into
                focus when nobody else could.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- New C -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option C stacked with photo left">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">C · Stacked, photo left</p>
      <div class="tc-stack">
        <div class="tcard tc-card">
          <div class="tcard-inner">
            <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Photo</span>
            <div>
              <p class="q">
                Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
                decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make
                it, then she stays until it lands.
              </p>
              <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tc-card">
          <div class="tcard-inner">
            <span class="ph" aria-hidden="true">Photo</span>
            <div>
              <p class="q">
                She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the
                room hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that
                had never questioned the plan started asking which one thing
                mattered most.
              </p>
              <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
